WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.171 --> 00:00:06.240
Speaker 1: Earlier this week, I told you that&nbsp;
Rudy Giuliani and John Eastman, two former&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:11.440
Donald Trump lawyers and Republican Senator&nbsp;
Lindsey Graham, have all been subpoenaed by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:19.200
a court in the state of Georgia. And it's become&nbsp;
very common for Republicans to ignore subpoenas&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:24.240
from Congress to appear before the January six&nbsp;
committee. But ignoring a subpoena from a court&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:29.040
is a very different thing. Well, we've now&nbsp;
heard from Republican Senator Lindsey Graham.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:33.600
He says he's not going to cooperate with the&nbsp;
Georgia Trump election probe. Now, importantly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:37.440
some of you wrote to me and said, how can Lindsey&nbsp;
get away with this? This isn't he going to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:42.400
thrown in jail for contempt of court? Understand,&nbsp;
Lindsey is not saying he's going to ignore it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:47.360
He's saying he's going to fight it. He's going to&nbsp;
try to fight the subpoena. Senator Lindsey Graham&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:52.320
reports. Reuters will not comply with a subpoena&nbsp;
issued by a grand jury in Georgia investigating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:57.360
Trump's attempts to overturn the results of the&nbsp;
2020 elections. Quote Senator Graham plans to go&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.360 --> 00:01:03.680
to court to challenge the subpoena and expects to&nbsp;
prevail, said, I guess, two of his attorneys. They&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:08.720
say Graham was well within his rights to discuss&nbsp;
with state officials the processes and procedures&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:15.440
around administering elections. What they're&nbsp;
referring to is that Graham called and you know,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:20.080
it was very clear he was trying to strong&nbsp;
arm Georgia into flipping the results.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:23.200
But what they're calling it is&nbsp;
a discussion about procedures.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:29.680
Very benign way to refer to it. The grand jury&nbsp;
also subpoenaed Rudy Giuliani and others. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.680 --> 00:01:33.600
grand jury was selected in May to look at&nbsp;
evidence in a probe launched after Trump&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:38.400
was recorded on a phone call pressuring&nbsp;
state officials to overturn the results.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:43.040
Graham's attorney said in the statement that&nbsp;
the senator was being called simply as a witness&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:47.440
in what they call a fishing expedition. Any&nbsp;
information from an interview or a deposition with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:51.120
Senator Graham would immediately be shared with&nbsp;
the January six committee. They don't like that.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.720 --> 00:02:00.320
And he is going to try to fight the subpoena. Now,&nbsp;
if he tries to fight the subpoena and loses and a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:07.360
court says you have to respond to the subpoena,&nbsp;
and he doesn't. He would then be in contempt of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:12.720
court. That is not where we are right now. If&nbsp;
the court decides he must comply and he doesn't,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:17.760
it will become a legal issue for him. Unlikely.&nbsp;
I have to tell you that he will end up arrested&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:23.920
because he's not again, he's not a subject or&nbsp;
a target of the investigation. He's merely a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.920 --> 00:02:29.200
witness. He still could be held in contempt.&nbsp;
He could face daily fines. If he ignores it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:34.240
it's not likely that he's going to be imprisoned.&nbsp;
And if he still didn't pay the fines that are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.240 --> 00:02:39.600
assigned to him for ignoring the subpoena,&nbsp;
then his assets could be seized. But it is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:44.720
very unlikely that Lindsey is actually going to&nbsp;
get himself arrested. That's where we are right&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:50.080
now. Of course, it would be great if everybody&nbsp;
just complied and they could tell us everything&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:54.720
we need to know. And it would be very clear that&nbsp;
everybody is innocent, nobody did anything wrong,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.720 --> 00:02:59.600
and then we could just all move on with our lives.&nbsp;
But instead they are obstructing and impeding and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.600 --> 00:03:05.440
trying to get in the way of these investigations&nbsp;
at every turn. I will remind you, my opinion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.440 --> 00:03:11.440
remains that it is more likely that if there are&nbsp;
going to be big time charges even against Trump,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.440 --> 00:03:16.000
which I don't think is particularly likely, but&nbsp;
if it's going to happen, I believe it's far more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:21.760
likely to come from the Georgia investigation&nbsp;
than from the January six investigation. And I've&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:29.120
given the reasons why already, and that's where my&nbsp;
mind remains. Obviously, if they don't get people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.120 --> 00:03:34.400
to comply with subpoenas, it will be much more&nbsp;
difficult to build these cases. We will have more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:40.640
on all of these stories on The David Pakman Show&nbsp;
Instagram, which can be found at David Pakman show

